From 41a12fc75d6b1a7f2cf422611b25ebc458074b01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 18:20:24 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 046/141] kernel: Random Walk (Legacy) was missing from the
 closure skip table

Found while looking for the cause of the black subsurface render:
svm_node_closure_bsdf_skip() lists the three other BSSRDF methods -- burley,
random_walk, random_walk_skin -- but not random_walk_legacy, which fell into the
default case and advanced the SVM stream by sizeof(SVMNodeSimpleBsdfData)
instead of sizeof(SVMNodeBssrdfData), several uints too short.

This function is not a rare case: it is called whenever a closure has to be
skipped rather than evaluated -- zero mix weight, volume shading pass, a
feature mask that is neither BSDF nor emission. Choosing Random Walk (Legacy)
and reaching one of these paths made the rest of the SVM stream read garbage.

A bug independent of Houdini, in the kernel itself -- present as is on
Blender's main branch at the time of the rebase. One-line fix: add the missing
case to the group of the other three.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kernel/svm/closure.h | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/kernel/svm/closure.h b/src/kernel/svm/closure.h
index 311bcf02..dd31a2bf 100644
--- a/src/kernel/svm/closure.h
+++ b/src/kernel/svm/closure.h
@@ -79,7 +79,14 @@ ccl_device_inline int svm_node_closure_bsdf_skip(int offset, const uint type)
       break;
     case CLOSURE_BSSRDF_BURLEY_ID:
     case CLOSURE_BSSRDF_RANDOM_WALK_ID:
+    case CLOSURE_BSSRDF_RANDOM_WALK_LEGACY_ID:
     case CLOSURE_BSSRDF_RANDOM_WALK_SKIN_ID:
+      /* Random Walk (Legacy) was missing here: it fell to the `default` case
+       * below and advanced `offset` by sizeof(SVMNodeSimpleBsdfData), several
+       * uints short of the actual SVMNodeBssrdfData it was written with. Every
+       * skip of that closure - a zero mix weight, a volume shading pass, any
+       * feature mask that is neither BSDF nor emission - misread everything
+       * the SVM stream held after it. */
       offset += sizeof(SVMNodeBssrdfData) / sizeof(uint);
       break;
     default:
